---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Conscious Form">
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    
    {/* Header with optional photo */}
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 mb-12">
      
      {/* Photo - replace src with your actual photo */}
      <div class="w-48 h-48 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-neutral-800 flex-shrink-0 mx-auto md:mx-0">
        <img 
          src="/images/headshot.jpg" 
          alt="Darren Woodland, Jr."
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
        {/* If no photo yet, comment out img and uncomment below */}
        {/* <div class="w-full h-full flex items-center justify-center text-neutral-600">Photo</div> */}
      </div>
      
      {/* Intro */}
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Darren Woodland, Jr.</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-neutral-400 mb-4">
          Creative Technologist · Technical Artist
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
          I build real-time 3D, XR and sensor-driven systems for performance, exhibition
          and learning. Most of my projects start from something physical, a vessel of
          water or a dancer's motion capture, and end in Unreal, Unity, Houdini or Max/MSP.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Bio sections */}
    <div class="space-y-8 text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Practice</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          On <em>Black Ice</em>, a VR film that premiered at SXSW 2022 and screened in the
          SIGGRAPH 2022 VR Theater, I was art director and technical artist: I designed,
          modeled and sourced the assets and implemented all of the audio in Wwise. For
          BioreactAR, an AR passthrough teaching tool for Quest 3, I was the primary Unity
          developer. Dance companies at Drexel and in Denver have staged their work in front
          of animated scenography I built in Houdini and Unreal Engine.
        </p>
        <p>
          My dissertation is three instruments. One reads vibration in a box of soil and
          rock, another reads the chemistry of water as earthen orbs dissolve in it, and
          the third reads hair by touch and by camera; each one drives a composition in
          Max/MSP. Collaboration fills the rest of my record, usually with me responsible
          for the technical side: AR pieces for another artist's exhibition, and gesture
          systems for a robotics lab.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Background</h2>
        <p>
          I am a PhD candidate in Digital Media at Drexel University, finishing in 2027,
          with a graduate minor in computer science. There I teach scripting, game
          development and technical art, and administer the college's Perforce server.
          Alongside the PhD, the Robotics, Automation, and Dance (RAD) Lab hosts me as
          Artist in Residence, where I prototype gesture-based interaction for human-robot
          interaction research. Earlier, at NC State's IntelliMedia Group, I made 2D and 3D
          assets for educational games and VR training while finishing an M.A.D. in
          Experimental Media Arts. My work has been presented at Ars Electronica and
          published at SIGGRAPH Asia.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Tools</h2>
        <p>
          Unreal Engine (Blueprints, Sequencer, C++ for scripting) and Unity (C#, URP,
          Meta XR SDK) for real-time and XR. Houdini and Maya for modeling, simulation and
          animation, with Python for scripting and cleanup. Max/MSP, PlugData and Wwise for
          audio. ESP32, Teensy and Arduino for sensors, with OpenCV and vvvv for computer
          vision. Perforce and Git for version control.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400">
          <a href="mailto:darrenwoodland3@gmail.com" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">
            darrenwoodland3@gmail.com
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>